60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option A needs deep digging. The clay will slip. The boardwalks will sink. It is too risky.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B matches the data. People want open, firm ground. The paved square is logical.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option C has too many trees. The seven staff cannot prune them all. It is too much work.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option A is a trap. The reeds will die like the avenue trees. The water will clog.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is a financial black hole. The fund pays for the water, but the city pays for the boardwalks.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,Option D is simple. Concrete and courts. The ground can take it. The firms can build it fast.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Option D is good for the ground. But the data shows people walk through, not to play.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,Option B is easy. The volunteers can sweep the square. The staff can check the stalls.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,Option B is honest. It is hard to break. It does not need watering. It will last.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B is the only one that does not create a new maintenance line. The fund covers nothing, but the city pays little.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I am leaning toward D. It is safe for the soil. But I worry about the heat.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the heat is a problem for plants, not for concrete. Option B is the logical choice.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,I like Option B. It is simple. The volunteers can help with the cleaning. It feels peaceful.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,I choose Option B. It is the only one that respects the history of neglect. It will stand.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I choose Option B. It is the only one that does not promise a future the city cannot afford.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I will vote for D. It is the safest for the ground. I cannot risk the slip.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will vote for B. It matches the usage. It is the rational choice.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I will vote for B. It is kind to the staff. It is kind to the volunteers.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,I will vote for B. It is the only one that will still be there in ten years.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for B. It is the only one that does not become a debt.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
